  "notes": "Round one (078): triage group (9)'s light beams, visions-25.jpg the default; splendor (jade_starbursts), sparx (moss_starbursts), state-of-being (garnet_starbursts) and treasury (gilt_starbursts) as palette entries (tone only). Straight beams do not come from one escape loop (052: a loop draws arcs along the arms), so the beams are the post stage's new `rays` pass (POST.md): the brightest 0.15% of the frame casts six spokes from 15 degrees (none upright: at 90 the first cut's one-sample spokes read as rain; the 135 and 315 pair are one-sample diagonals, which read as crisp star points), each fading over 0.08 frame widths, tinted the map's 0.9. What casts is the stack's own sparkle (gaussian_int sparks masked to the set by inverted de at power 6) and the set's hair, so every star sits on the fractal. Under it, soft_veils' reading in three loops (scooped sheets of the smooth count and stripe wisps, the frame's and two views) and a dark interior. Nearest mode: soft_veils (veils); the stars are what differ. Round one's lessons: unmasked sparks cast a cross-hatch screen over the whole frame; untinted beams summed over four spokes wash the violet to grey; the beams want seats whose sparks cluster (phoenix seats read best). Readings: cross (four spokes at 45), long (0.15), flare (a second pass: the brightest 0.01% casting a long four-spoke X), burst (radial shafts from the middle under the stars), white (beams in their source's colour), no_rays (the headline off). Tone, round one: 25 of 35 scout drafts hold (10 of the 12 kept seats); every miss is p90 (0.50 to 0.60 against 0.403) at star clusters and lace-dense seats. Cost: 66.5 s as WebAssembly on one thread at 1280x800 ss2 at phoenix_2d843082 (maxiter 9,266), the rays pass 7.3 s of it.",
